Here is a minimal counter.

```tsx
'use client';
import { useState } from 'react';
export function Counter() {
  const [n, setN] = useState(0);
  return <button onClick={() => setN(n + 1)}>{n}</button>;
}
```

Use semantic forms for mutations and accessibility.

```tsx
export function ContactForm() {
  return (
    <form action="/api/contact" method="post">
      <label htmlFor="email">Email</label>
      <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required />
      <button type="submit">Send</button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

A Server Component renders on the server by default in the App Router.

```tsx
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetchData();
  return <main>{data.title}</main>;
}
```

No useState or useEffect in server files.

Use useEffect with an abort controller for race-safe fetching.

```tsx
'use client';
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
export function UserCard({ id }: { id: string }) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    const c = new AbortController();
    fetch(`/api/users/${id}`, { signal: c.signal }).then(r => r.json()).then(setUser);
    return () => c.abort();
  }, [id]);
  return <div>{user?.name}</div>;
}

Wire zodResolver into useForm and render field errors.

```tsx
const schema = z.object({ email: z.string().email() });
const form = useForm({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) });
// ...
<input {...form.register('email')} />
```

The resolver keeps client validation aligned with the schema.

Compose small slot components with children.

```tsx
export function Card({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <div className="rounded border p-4">{children}</div>;
}
export function CardBody({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <div className="mt-2">{children}</div>;
}
```

Usage:
```tsx
<Card>
  <CardBody>Title</CardBody>
  {/* ... */}
</Card>
```

Mark server modules explicitly and never import them in client files.

```ts
import 'server-only';
export const db = /* ... */;
```

Client bundles must not pull server-only code.

Route handlers live under app/api.

```ts
export async function GET() {
  const rows = await db.query();
  // ...
  return Response.json(rows);
}
```

Keep side effects server-side only.

